 "notes": "The west face of the Escampobariou headland at the tip of the Giens peninsula; coastline and lighthouse from OpenStreetMap. The dive-site position (43.031848, 6.096302) and the mooring on a buoy flush with the cliff just before the Pointe d'Escampobariou come from the Var tourist board (Provence Méditerranée) sheet, which also gives the drop-off to about 40 m; the posidonia flat on the shoulder and the rocks come from first-hand observation. The drop-off line, seagrass area and route are schematic; the sea caves the sheet mentions are not placed because their position was not found.",
